## Blog

- [AI Functions in ClickHouse: Upgrade your SQL to the AI age](https://clickhouse.com/blog/ai-functions-in-clickhouse): Explore ClickHouse AI Functions for classification, generation, translation, embeddings, semantic search, and cost controls—all directly from SQL.
- [Introducing WalShadow: Sub-second Postgres replication to ClickHouse from physical WAL](https://clickhouse.com/blog/introducing-walshadow): WalShadow replicates Postgres data directly from physical WAL into ClickHouse, delivering around 200 ms latency and 289,000 rows per second in benchmarks.
- [ClickHouse is a launch partner for the Data agent in ChatGPT Work](https://clickhouse.com/blog/chatgpt-data-plugin): ClickHouse joins the Data agent in ChatGPT Work, connecting ClickHouse Cloud to natural-language queries, reports, and interactive dashboards.
- [Announcing On-Demand Compute: Instant compute for your most intensive workloads](https://clickhouse.com/blog/on-demand-compute): ClickHouse On-Demand Compute lets you scale individual queries with additional workers, run intensive workloads without disrupting production, and use compute when you need it.
- [Loading Parquet data into MySQL with ClickHouse](https://clickhouse.com/blog/parquet-to-mysql-with-clickhouse): Use ClickHouse to load Parquet files into MySQL, explore remote data, and run MySQL queries with table functions and named collections.
- [ClickHouse release 26.8](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickhouse-release-26-08): ClickHouse 26.8 LTS introduces background queries, pipelined SQL, new text tokenizers, expanded data lake integrations, and faster Parquet, aggregation, and join queries.
- [ClickHouse Cloud vs. Snowflake: What drives the real-time performance-per-dollar gap](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickhouse-vs-snowflake-real-time-performance-per-dollar): ClickHouse Cloud delivered 412× better performance per dollar than Snowflake in CostBench. We trace the gap from fresh data arriving to fast answers coming back.
- [Announcing ClickHouse Managed Postgres on Google Cloud](https://clickhouse.com/blog/postgres-managed-by-clickhouse-gcp-private-preview): ClickHouse Managed Postgres is expanding to Google Cloud, bringing NVMe-backed storage, native CDC into ClickHouse, and a unified query layer via pg_clickhouse to GCP private preview customers.
- [Introducing chdb Postgres extension: High-performance imports from cloud storage](https://clickhouse.com/blog/introducing-chdb-postgres): The chdb Postgres extension brings fast imports and exports across cloud storage platforms and data formats, powered by the embedded ClickHouse engine.
- [Measuring real-time performance per dollar under continuous load: CostBench’s first end-to-end results](https://clickhouse.com/blog/costbench-real-time-performance-per-dollar): CostBench puts cloud data warehouses under continuous load. Across the complete path from fresh data to fast answers, ClickHouse Cloud delivers 412–1,996× better performance per dollar.
- [How MCP Toolbox turns agent text into ClickHouse vectors](https://clickhouse.com/blog/mcp-toolbox-clickhouse-vectors): Google's MCP Toolbox for Databases embeds agent text into vectors on insert and search, then lets ClickHouse rank the results - no embedding service to build or maintain. Here's how to set it up, and what it looks like end to end.
- [ClickHouse as a streaming HTTP API](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickhouse-streaming-http-api): Learn how to build a streaming HTTP API directly in ClickHouse 26.8 with named handlers, typed parameters, pagination, framing formats, and access control.
- [Pipelined SQL in ClickHouse 26.8](https://clickhouse.com/blog/pipelined-sql-26.8): Learn how ClickHouse 26.8’s pipelined SQL syntax lets you build multi-stage queries as a readable sequence of transformations.
- [Build a real-time market data app with ClickHouse and Massive](https://clickhouse.com/blog/build-a-real-time-market-data-app-with-clickhouse-and-polygonio): Learn how to build a real-time financial analytics application with Massive and ClickHouse that scales to thousands of events per second.
- [Introducing Scheduled Upgrades in ClickHouse Managed Postgres](https://clickhouse.com/blog/introducing-scheduled-upgrades-in-clickhouse-managed-postgres): ClickHouse Managed Postgres now supports scheduled upgrade windows, giving Scale and Enterprise users more control over when routine platform maintenance occurs.
- [MySQL CDC connector for ClickPipes is now Generally Available](https://clickhouse.com/blog/mysql-cdc-connector-for-clickpipes-is-now-generally-available): Replicate MySQL and MariaDB data into ClickHouse Cloud with the generally available MySQL CDC connector, featuring faster parallel snapshots, safer production defaults, improved observability, and infrastructure-as-code support.
- [From Neon Postgres to ClickHouse Managed Postgres](https://clickhouse.com/blog/neon-to-clickhouse-managed-postgres): Three teams share why they migrated production Postgres workloads from Neon to ClickHouse Managed Postgres and how ClickPipes helped them cut over in hours.
- [ClickHouse welcomes RunReveal](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickhouse-welcomes-runreveal): Security is the largest and fastest growing data workload in the enterprise, and today, ClickHouse has acquired RunReveal.
- [The Agentic Analytics Benchmark: Measuring model accuracy and efficiency in analytical agents](https://clickhouse.com/blog/agentic-analytics-benchmark-data-agent-mnist): We took 201 real analytics questions from our production data warehouse, benchmarked 29 models on correctness, cost, and speed, and released an open harness so you can run the same test on your own.
- [How Uken Games reduces observability costs by 87% with ClickHouse](https://clickhouse.com/blog/uken-games-clickhouse-observability-stack): Uken Games replaced Datadog with an open-source observability stack built on ClickHouse, cutting costs by 87% while storing every trace on a single node.
- [New system views in PostgreSQL 19](https://clickhouse.com/blog/postgres-19-new-system-views): PostgreSQL 19 adds four system views that make lock contention, recovery state, autovacuum priorities, and dynamic shared memory allocations easier to inspect.
- [A new getting started experience for ClickHouse Managed Postgres](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickhouse-managed-postgres-onboarding): See how a four-step onboarding flow helps users move from provisioning ClickHouse Managed Postgres to querying operational data and running real-time analytics with ClickHouse.
- [So, is ClickHouse winning the observability wars?](https://clickhouse.com/blog/is-clickhouse-winning-the-observability-wars): After claims that ClickHouse is “winning the observability wars” sparked debate, we reflect on why it has become a leading storage and query engine, where it still falls short, and why winning the database layer isn’t the same as winning observability.
- [A universal interface: How QuintoAndar made ClickHouse plug-and-play with managed Postgres](https://clickhouse.com/blog/quintoandar-managed-postgres): QuintoAndar unified ~900 million monthly events in ClickHouse Cloud and used ClickHouse Managed Postgres to make that data accessible to Hightouch and any Postgres-compatible tool.
- [What's new in the ClickHouse .NET Driver: the road from 1.0 to 1.3](https://clickhouse.com/blog/whats-new-clickhouse-net-driver-10-to-13): Discover how ClickHouse .NET Driver 1.1–1.3 adds type-safe POCO workflows, extensible serialization, broader type support, performance improvements, and official ecosystem integrations.
- [How Suprema Gaming made its data platform agent-ready with ClickHouse Cloud](https://clickhouse.com/blog/suprema-gaming-agent-ready-platform): Suprema Gaming migrated its analytics platform from Snowflake to ClickHouse Cloud to power a company-wide shift toward agentic operations.
- [Read your writes: WAIT FOR in PostgreSQL 19](https://clickhouse.com/blog/postgresql-19-wait-for-read-your-writes): PostgreSQL 19's new `WAIT FOR` command enables read-your-writes consistency on asynchronous replicas by letting individual reads wait for a specific WAL position.
- [ClickGap: Autonomous QA for ClickHouse](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickgap-autonomous-qa-for-clickhouse): ClickGap reviews merged ClickHouse changes, executes reproducers, rejects false positives, and attributes regressions to specific commits.
- [Ensuring reliable OpenTelemetry ingestion at scale](https://clickhouse.com/blog/reliable-opentelemetry-ingestion-at-scale): How ClickHouse Cloud collects 50m events per second through OpenTelemetry
- [What else runs on your Postgres server, and how do we stop it from taking the database down?](https://clickhouse.com/blog/protect-postgres-from-supporting-processes): ClickHouse Managed Postgres uses runtime budgets, cgroup limits, and disk-full session exemptions to keep supporting services from compromising database availability.
- [August 2026 newsletter](https://clickhouse.com/blog/202608-newsletter): Welcome to the August 2026 ClickHouse newsletter, which will round up what’s happened in real-time data warehouses over the last month.
- [POSETTE Talk Recap - Postgres Isn't Slow. Your Storage Is](https://clickhouse.com/blog/posette-talk-recap-postgres-isnt-slow-your-storage-is): A recap of Sai Srirampur's POSETTE 2026 talk on storage performance in Postgres, with a local NVMe vs. EBS benchmark and the production setup behind it.
- [Shopify powers observability for global-scale commerce with ClickHouse](https://clickhouse.com/blog/shopify-observability-at-global-scale): Shopify unified global-scale observability on ClickHouse, achieving up to 30x faster queries while ingesting 100 million events per second at peak.
- [How Sony LIV uses ClickHouse Cloud to deliver live streaming analytics at billion-row scale](https://clickhouse.com/blog/sony-liv-real-time-analytics): Sony LIV consolidated fragmented batch, Elasticsearch, and BigQuery workloads on ClickHouse Cloud, delivering sub-second analytics across billions of daily streaming events.
- [What's New with Monitoring in PostgreSQL 19](https://clickhouse.com/blog/postgres-19-monitoring-whats-new): What's New with Monitoring in PostgreSQL 19
- [Announcing support for ClickStack in the ClickHouse Terraform provider](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickstack-terraform-provider): The ClickHouse Terraform provider now manages ClickStack dashboards, alerts, sources, and webhooks, putting observability config in version control.
- [What’s new in the ClickHouse Grafana plugin](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickhouse-grafana-plugin-4-20): ClickHouse Grafana plugin 4.20 brings compact query mode, click-to-filter log investigation, guided variable and annotation editors, and OpenTelemetry dashboards
- [ClickStack and Hud bring runtime intelligence to AI-powered development](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickstack-hud-runtime-intelligence): ClickStack and Hud now share trace IDs, pairing service-level observability with function-level runtime forensics so coding agents can assess risky changes before they ship, catch regressions right after deploy, and fix them with real production context.
- [How iFood built its agentic security platform on ClickHouse Cloud](https://clickhouse.com/blog/ifood-agentic-security-platform): iFood rebuilt its in-house security platform on ClickHouse Cloud, getting 9-16x faster queries at 40-50% of the cost and unlocking agentic threat hunts that cut a week of analyst work down to two hours.
- [What's new in pg_clickhouse v0.10.0: Subqueries, TPC-H Speedups, C Driver, and Aggregates](https://clickhouse.com/blog/pg_clickhouse-whats-new-july-2026): Discover what's new in pg_clickhouse v0.10.0: 16 of 22 TPC-H queries now push down in full, plus a rebuilt C driver and broader aggregate support.
- [bitdrift brings ClickHouse-powered mobile observability to ClickStack](https://clickhouse.com/blog/bitdrift-clickhouse-mobile-observability-for-clickstack): bitdrift joins ClickHouse’s House Mates program with a mobile observability integration, bringing mobile-native telemetry, tracing, and debugging to ClickStack.
- [Whats new in ClickStack - June + July](https://clickhouse.com/blog/whats-new-in-clickstack-june-2026): Explore ClickStack’s latest upgrades, from richer trace navigation and Prometheus connectivity to smarter dashboards, quieter alerts, faster filtering and support for exponential histogram metrics.
- [How Musinsa scaled its audience engine with ClickHouse Cloud and reduced TCO by 71.4%](https://clickhouse.com/blog/musinsa-customer-data-platform): Musinsa migrated its audience engine from self-hosted ClickHouse to ClickHouse Cloud, cutting storage costs by 86.5% and total cost of ownership by up to 71.4% while simplifying real-time ingestion with ClickPipes.
- [What's new in ClickHouse Managed Postgres: Customer notifications, better observability, faster backups, extensions, and more](https://clickhouse.com/blog/managed-postgres-notifications-observability-backups): Explore the latest ClickHouse Managed Postgres updates, including proactive notifications, richer observability, faster backups, and expanded extension support.
- [ClickHouse Release 26.7](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickhouse-release-26-07): This release brings speedups for GROUP BY ... ORDER BY ... LIMIT, three JOIN improvements, four vector search improvements, position-aware phrase search, EXPLAIN ANALYZE, unified URL access, and more!
- [How Physical Intelligence unified its robotics data stack with Postgres managed by ClickHouse](https://clickhouse.com/blog/physical-intelligence-rds-to-clickhouse-managed-postgres): Physical Intelligence runs both its OLAP and OLTP workloads on ClickHouse managed Postgres and ClickHouse Cloud
- [What is WAL backpressure, and why does ClickHouse Managed Postgres need it?](https://clickhouse.com/blog/wal-backpressure-clickhouse-managed-postgres): How ClickHouse Managed Postgres uses WAL-aware backpressure to slow client writes, protect disk space, and let the archiver recover.
- [How Mercado Libre rebuilt its observability platform on ClickHouse Cloud with 50x faster trace queries](https://clickhouse.com/blog/mercado-libre-observability-on-clickhouse-cloud): How Mercado Libre rebuilt its observability platform on ClickHouse Cloud, cutting trace query times from over five minutes to about four seconds (a 50x speedup) with up to 89% compression while ingesting 400 million spans per minute.
- [Fixed cadence to seconds: making ClickHouse Cloud autoscaling more reactive](https://clickhouse.com/blog/making-clickhouse-cloud-autoscaling-more-reactive): How we rebuilt ClickHouse Cloud's autoscaling orchestration on Kubernetes' controller-runtime and a ClickHouse-powered signals table, adding a reactive fast path that scales services up in seconds instead of waiting for the next scheduled pass.
- [ClickHouse launches ClickHouse Labs with Andy Pavlo as VP of Database Research](https://clickhouse.com/blog/andy-pavlo-founding-clickhouse-labs): Renowned database researcher will lead a new group dedicated to advancing foundational database technology and sharing its work openly with the broader community.
- [Andy Pavlo joins ClickHouse to establish ClickHouse Labs](https://clickhouse.com/blog/andy-pavlo-joins-clickhouse): I am excited to announce that I am joining ClickHouse, Inc. to establish and lead a new research team at ClickHouse Labs.
- [I created a playground for 110 database systems](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickbench-playground): You can choose any of these hundred database systems and run queries. You can create tables and databases, insert data, drop tables, etc. Every database comes with a preloaded dataset of 100 million records, so you can test example queries. It has not onl
- [What's new in clickhousectl v0.4.0](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickhousectl-v0-4-0): clickhousectl v0.4.0 adds horizontal autoscaling for Cloud services, ClickPipe schema discovery, finer control over ClickPipe ingestion, and opt-out anonymous usage telemetry.
- [ClickHouse joins the Open Secure AI Alliance](https://clickhouse.com/blog/open-secure-ai-alliance): ClickHouse is joining the Open Secure AI Alliance alongside NVIDIA and other industry leaders to help build open tools that keep AI agents secure.
- [Choosing Between ClickStack and Grafana for ClickHouse Observability](https://clickhouse.com/blog/choosing-between-clickstack-and-grafana-for-clickhouse-observability): Using ClickHouse for observability and wondering which interface best fits your workflows? We explore ClickStack, Grafana, and when it makes sense to use both.
- [Benchmarking NVMe-backed Managed Postgres: PlanetScale and ClickHouse](https://clickhouse.com/blog/benchmarking-nvme-managed-postgres-planetscale-vs-clickhouse): We ran ClickHouse Managed Postgres and PlanetScale on the same hardware. ClickHouse delivered up to 54% higher throughput with lower latency.
- [How Jump Trading uses ClickHouse with Iceberg for analytics](https://clickhouse.com/blog/jump-trading-uses-clickhouse-with-iceberg): Jump Trading captures petabyte-scale financial trading logs on a self-managed ClickHouse platform, where zero data loss and low latency are critical requirements.
- [Instrumenting my espresso machine with OpenTelemetry](https://clickhouse.com/blog/espresso-machine-observability-with-otel): Treating a Gaggia espresso machine like a distributed system: instrumenting an ESP32 with OpenTelemetry, streaming shots and whole-house sensors into ClickHouse Cloud, and putting ClickStack (plus an LLM agent) on top to turn every pull into a queryable,
- [How Fetch built its flexible agentic analytics tool on ClickHouse Cloud](https://clickhouse.com/blog/fetch-agentic-analytics): Fetch built FAST, a conversational BI agent on ClickHouse Cloud, so non-technical teams can query 150 billion rows a day in plain language and get answers in minutes instead of days.
- [Why strict memory overcommit matters for Postgres](https://clickhouse.com/blog/strict-memory-overcommit-for-postgres): Why ClickHouse Managed Postgres runs strict memory overcommit by default, and how it turns an instance-wide OOM restart into a single failed query — shown side by side on identical hardware, with no measurable throughput cost.
- [ClickHouse docs relaunch](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickhouse-docs-on-mintlify): We have relaunched clickhouse.com/docs on Mintlify, with a redesigned search and Ask AI experience, a docs MCP server, simpler navigation, an interactive API playground, and expanded localization — built for both human readers and the coding agents
- [ClickHouse achieves AWS Small and Medium Business Competency](https://clickhouse.com/blog/achieves-aws-smb-competency): ClickHouse has achieved the AWS Small and Medium Business Competency, joining a select group of AWS Partners recognized for deep expertise in real-time analytics for small and medium businesses.
- [Agentic infrastructure with clickhousectl: a distributed ClickStack across three continents](https://clickhouse.com/blog/agentic-infrastructure-clickhousectl-distributed-clickstack): How a coding agent used clickhousectl to stand up a distributed ClickStack across the US, Europe, and Japan, with regional ingestion and one global view.
- [How we build and evaluate our MCP server for SRE agents](https://clickhouse.com/blog/benchmarking-the-clickstack-mcp-server-with-hdx-evals): A behind-the-scenes look at hdx-evals, the open-source framework we built to benchmark the ClickStack MCP server against a raw SQL baseline using deterministic synthetic incidents, sandboxed Claude agents, and blind LLM grading — and why the MCP scored hi
- [Migrate Datadog telemetry with the OpenTelemetry Collector](https://clickhouse.com/blog/datadog-receiver-opentelemetry-collector): Recent improvements to the OpenTelemetry Collector's Datadog receiver let teams reroute telemetry from their existing Datadog agents and SDKs to ClickStack. or any OTel destination making migrations and evaluations simpler than ever.
- [PostgresBench: Measuring the impact of High Availability on Managed Postgres performance](https://clickhouse.com/blog/postgresbench-ha): PostgresBench now includes HA benchmarks, comparing the performance of managed Postgres services under production-style HA configurations. This post explains the architectures behind each service and analyzes the trade-offs between availability guarantees
- [ClickHouse announced as Principal Partner and Front of Shirt Sponsor of Fulham Football Club](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickhouse-announced-principal-partner-sponsor-fulham-fc): Fulham Football Club is proud to announce ClickHouse, a global technology company specialising in real-time analytics, data infrastructure and AI applications, as its newest Principal Partner and Front of Shirt Sponsor of the Men’s First Team.
- [July 2026 newsletter](https://clickhouse.com/blog/202607-newsletter): Welcome to the July 2026 ClickHouse newsletter, which will round up what’s happened in real-time data warehouses over the last month.
- [Why Trainy migrated from Amazon RDS Postgres to ClickHouse Managed Postgres](https://clickhouse.com/blog/trainy-postgres-managed-by-clickhouse): Trainy moved Pluto's metadata layer from Amazon RDS to ClickHouse Managed Postgres, cutting costs and making page loads up to 3x faster while unifying OLAP and OLTP under one vendor.
- [Replacing the HDB: ClickHouse for historical ticker data](https://clickhouse.com/blog/historical-ticker-data): A hands-on walkthrough of loading billions of Binance tick records into ClickHouse, showing how columnar storage and codecs compress trade and quote data 19x, and how standard SQL handles VWAP, OHLC candles, and as-of joins at millisecond granularity.
- [How Bullet uses ClickHouse Cloud to give DeFi's fastest exchange real-time analytics](https://clickhouse.com/blog/bullet-real-time-analytics): Switching from Databricks to ClickHouse Cloud cut Bullet's query latency 10,000x and eliminated an entire serving layer, giving DeFi's fastest exchange real-time analytics at comparable cost.
- [@clickhouse/rowbinary: when your library is also a parser compiler](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickhouse-rowbinary-library-parser-compiler): We've released @clickhouse/rowbinary a Node.js reader and writer for ClickHouse's RowBinary formats. You can import it and call its generic parser like any other library. But it also ships as an Agent Skill: point a coding agent at the bundled `SKILL.md`
- [How we configure huge pages in ClickHouse Managed Postgres](https://clickhouse.com/blog/huge-pages-clickhouse-managed-postgres): How ClickHouse Managed Postgres reserves, enforces, and sizes huge pages so shared_buffers avoids the per-connection page-table tax that eats RAM and stalls reads on 4KB pages.
- [How Insider One uses ClickHouse Cloud to power real-time customer engagement at scale](https://clickhouse.com/blog/insiderone-customer-data-platform): Insider One cut query latency by up to 75% and eliminated operational overhead by moving its Unified Customer Database from self-managed ClickHouse to ClickHouse Cloud.
- [ClickHouse on Docker Hardened Images](https://clickhouse.com/blog/docker-hardened-images): ClickHouse is now available as a Docker Hardened Image: a minimal, security-hardened build that passes enterprise vulnerability scans by shipping only what the database needs to run, with no change to how ClickHouse behaves.
- [One Driver, One Format, Every Language: ADBC](https://clickhouse.com/blog/introducing-the-clickhouse-adbc-driver): ClickHouse now has an official ADBC driver, giving Ruby, R, C, and every other ADBC-aware tool zero-conversion, Arrow-native access to ClickHouse without a dedicated client for each language.
- [How Trigger.dev is using ClickHouse to scale observability for long-running AI workflows](https://clickhouse.com/blog/trigger-dev-scaling-observability): Trigger.dev migrated from Postgres to ClickHouse to scale observability for its serverless AI workflow platform, delivering ~200 ms P95 query performance and a dramatically smaller telemetry storage footprint.
- [Introducing pg_re2, fast, RE2-powered regular expressions in Postgres](https://clickhouse.com/blog/introducing-pg_re2-regex-in-postgres): Introducing pg_re2, a Postgres extension that brings ClickHouse's fast RE2-powered regular expressions to Postgres, with benchmarks and pg_clickhouse pushdown integration.
- [AI needs the best-of-breed data stack: Postgres and ClickHouse](https://clickhouse.com/blog/ai-best-of-breed-data-stack): AI applications are driving explosive data growth and collapsing the line between transactional and analytical workloads, making the best-of-breed combination of Postgres and ClickHouse — increasingly tied together through CDC, native querying, and observ
- [chDB as the Agent's Local Data Engine](https://clickhouse.com/blog/chdb-agents-local-data-engine): chDB embeds a full ClickHouse query engine inside an agent's own process, turning data access, memory, and federation into local function calls instead of network round trips, cutting the latency, retries, and token waste that come with remote queries.
- [98% faster queries, 50% lower cloud costs: Verihubs’ journey from Postgres to ClickHouse](https://clickhouse.com/blog/verihubs-data-warehouse): Verihubs rebuilt its Postgres data warehouse on ClickHouse with real-time Kafka streaming, cutting query times by up to 98% and cloud costs by up to 50%.
- [Introducing AI dashboard and workflow generation in ClickStack](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickstack-ai-dashboard-generation): ClickStack can now generate full dashboards and linked investigative workflows from a single prompt, using an AI Notebook and the same MCP tools available to external agents like Claude, Cursor, and Codex.
- [ClickHouse Release 26.6](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickhouse-release-26-06): ClickHouse 26.6 is here! In this release, we have hypothetical skip indexes, cascading refreshable materialized views, experimental support for continuous queries, and more!
- [How we made ClickStack 5x faster for ClickHouse observability](https://clickhouse.com/blog/making-clickstack-5x-faster-clickhouse-observability): Learn how the ClickStack team used a benchmark-driven process — combining primary key redesign, text indexes, alias columns, and materialized views — to reduce observability query latency by more than 5× ahead of general availability.
- [ClickHouse Agents is now available for Managed Postgres](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickhouse-agents-managed-postgres): ClickHouse Agents now connects directly to Managed Postgres, so you can query your operational data in plain English, combine it with ClickHouse in a single request, and get agent-guided help monitoring, tuning, and migrating your databases.
- [How we scale PgBouncer in ClickHouse Managed Postgres](https://clickhouse.com/blog/pgbouncer-clickhouse-managed-postgres): PgBouncer is single-threaded, so a single process caps out at one CPU core no matter the box size. See how ClickHouse Managed Postgres runs a peered fleet of PgBouncer processes with so_reuseport to scale pooling across every core — with benchmarks showin
- [How Artemis Security runs 69x faster detection queries with ClickHouse Cloud](https://clickhouse.com/blog/artemis-security-real-time-threat-detection): Artemis Security cut detection query times 69x and investigative lookups up to 60x using ClickHouse query coalescing, materialized extraction, and AI-powered debugging with Claude.
- [A Quadrillion Rows across three Clouds: scaling LogHouse](https://clickhouse.com/blog/a-quadrillion-rows-across-the-three-cloud-scaling-loghouse): We scaled our internal logging platform from 19 PiB to 431 PiB and 1.59 quadrillion rows. Here’s how we rearchitected LogHouse to handle 80 GiB/s of writes while keeping queries fast and the underlying complexity invisible.
- [Clever ingests 200x more logs at the same cost with ClickHouse Cloud](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clever-observability-at-scale): Clever replaced Datadog with ClickHouse Cloud and went from indexing 10% of their logs to 100%, gaining 200x more searchable log volume and 60 days of retention at no additional cost.
- [How Jua delivers the world’s most accurate physics simulations 3x faster with ClickHouse Cloud](https://clickhouse.com/blog/jua-physics-foundation-model): Jua replaced a file-based forecast pipeline with ClickHouse Cloud, cutting data delivery time from one hour to 20 minutes and historical query times from hours to seconds — giving energy traders a faster edge.
- [Agents hate friction: early thoughts on building for agents](https://clickhouse.com/blog/agents-hate-friction): We've had decades to learn what it means to design software and hardware for humans. How do we build experiences where the primary user may now be an LLM?
