- [June 2026 newsletter](https://clickhouse.com/blog/202606-newsletter): Welcome to the June 2026 ClickHouse newsletter, which will round up what’s happened in real-time data warehouses over the last month.
- [GCP Pub/Sub connector for ClickPipes is now in Private Preview](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickpipes-gcp-pub-sub-preview): Stream data from Pub/Sub in a few clicks for blazing-fast analytics over GCP infrastructure logs, application events, and operational signals. No routing through GCS or Dataflow required.
- [The open ecosystem around ClickHouse](https://clickhouse.com/blog/the-open-ecosystem-around-clickhouse): Around any good database sits the clients you import, the dashboards your team shares, the pipelines that feed it, the projects that build on top of it, and now the agents that query it.
- [92x faster queries: How Open Electricity uses ClickHouse to track Australia’s energy transition in real time](https://clickhouse.com/blog/openelectricity-australia-energy-transition): Open Electricity migrated ~1 billion rows of Australian energy data from Postgres and TimescaleDB to ClickHouse, achieving 92x faster queries on a fraction of the hardware.
- [What a difference 10 years of open source makes](https://clickhouse.com/blog/what-a-difference-10-years-of-open-source-makes): On June 15, 2016, ClickHouse went open source under the Apache 2.0 license. Ten years later, it's one of the most widely deployed analytical databases in the world.
- [Cisco Talos empowers threat researchers while reducing TCO by 75% with ClickHouse Cloud](https://clickhouse.com/blog/cisco): Cisco Talos runs a threat intelligence reputation service on ClickHouse Cloud, classifying file hashes so researchers can make fast, accurate security decisions.
- [Ten years of ClickHouse in open source](https://clickhouse.com/blog/open-source-10): ClickHouse was released in open source on Jun 15 2016, ten years ago. Since then, it became the most popular open source analytical database with more than 2000 contributors.
- [ClickHouse achieves AWS Retail Competency](https://clickhouse.com/blog/achieves-aws-retail-competency): ClickHouse has achieved the AWS Retail Competency, joining a select group of AWS Partners recognized for deep expertise in helping retailers turn live operational data into real-time decisions.
- [Introducing Postgres to Postgres ClickPipes in ClickHouse Cloud](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickpipes-postgres-to-postgres): Postgres to Postgres ClickPipes brings fully managed, low-downtime Postgres migrations to ClickHouse Cloud.
- [Building ClickCannon - a tool for benchmarking ClickHouse](https://clickhouse.com/blog/building-clickcannon-a-tool-for-benchmark-clickhouse): What started as an internal sizing tool for ClickStack became ClickCannon: an open-source framework for stress-testing ClickHouse with realistic data and user workloads.
- [Datadog and ClickHouse partner to bring full-fidelity data to modern observability](https://clickhouse.com/blog/datadog-and-clickhouse-partnership): ClickHouse and Datadog are partnering to combine full-fidelity log retention at scale with the powerful search and investigation experience engineers rely on every day.
- [Agents can now provision ClickHouse and Postgres on ClickHouse Cloud](https://clickhouse.com/blog/stripe-projects): One command in the Stripe CLI provisions a ClickHouse or Postgres service on ClickHouse Cloud and hands working credentials straight to your agent, with no UI or manual setup.
- [ClickHouse Agents: Claude-powered agentic analytics, now in public beta](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickhouse-agents-beta): text
- [How QRT powers real-time research and risk management at petabyte scale](https://clickhouse.com/blog/qrt): How QRT, a cloud-native quantitative investment manager, uses ClickHouse Cloud and ClickStack to power firm-wide research, real-time risk and P&L, and observability at petabyte scale.
- [What's new in clickhousectl v0.3.0](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickhousectl-v0-3-0): clickhousectl v0.3.0 brings a raft of improvements for the agentic experience, more ways to install, OAuth support for Query Endpoints, and custom configs.
- [ClickHouse appoints new leader for Asia Pacific and expands global go-to-market leadership team](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickhouse-appoints-apac-leader-and-expands-global-gtm-leadership): ClickHouse, a leader in real-time analytics, data warehousing, observability, and AI/ML, today announced an expansion of its global go-to-market (GTM) leadership team, including the appointment of Ed Lenta as Vice President, Asia Pacific and Japan (APJ).
- [Monitor SLAs and scale ClickHouse Cloud with clickhousectl and agents](https://clickhouse.com/blog/monitor-and-scale-clickhouse-cloud-with-clickhousectl): Tag queries to track per-workload SLAs, then use clickhousectl to investigate breaches and scale ClickHouse Cloud, with an agent to remediate.
- [What to look for when selecting a real-time analytical database](https://clickhouse.com/blog/selecting-a-real-time-analytical-database): Most databases can query fast. Far fewer can query data that arrived seconds ago. Learn what real-time analytics really requires.
- [Click-a-thon 2026: 24 hours, Bengaluru, and the fastest analytical database on the planet](https://clickhouse.com/blog/click-a-thon-2026): ClickHouse's first in-person hackathon in India. August 1–2, Bengaluru. Four tracks, ₹10,00,000 prize pool, 24 hours to ship something real. Applications close June 25.
- [Logging, Metrics, and Distributed Tracing in .NET with OpenTelemetry and ClickStack](https://clickhouse.com/blog/logging-metrics-distributed-tracing-dotnet-otel-clickstack): A walkthrough of adding OpenTelemetry instrumentation to two ASP.NET services — an Order API and a Payment Service — and shipping traces, logs, and metrics to ClickStack, with auto-correlated signals and cross-service trace waterfalls out of the box.
- [How ClickHouse became fast at joins](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickhouse-fast-joins): Over two years of focused join engineering, ClickHouse became 26× faster on the TPC-H SF100 join-heavy workload. Here’s how parallel hash joins, runtime filters, lazy column replication, and smarter join planning got us there.
- [Building a .NET API Gateway with ClickHouse and Aspire](https://clickhouse.com/blog/dotnet-api-gateway-aspire): A walkthrough of building a .NET API gateway with YARP and Aspire that logs every proxied request to ClickHouse for aggregate analytics, with a materialized view keeping dashboard queries fast as traffic grows.
- [TPC-H for less than a cent: ClickHouse Cloud vs. Snowflake, Databricks, BigQuery, and Redshift](https://clickhouse.com/blog/tpc-h-clickhouse-cloud-vs-snowflake-databricks-bigquery-redshift): ClickHouse Cloud takes on Snowflake, Databricks, BigQuery, and Redshift on TPC-H, ranking first on SF100 cost-performance and running SF10 for less than one cent.
- [ClickHouse Release 26.5](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickhouse-release-26-05): ClickHouse 26.5 is here! In this release, we have a record number of performance optimizations, a new `filesystem` table function for querying your local file system with SQL, and more!
- [Executable UDFs are now in public beta on ClickHouse Cloud](https://clickhouse.com/blog/executable-udfs-clickhouse-cloud-beta): Today we're excited to announce that executable UDFs are now available in public beta on ClickHouse Cloud. You can write a function in Python, upload it as a zip to your cluster, and call it from SQL like any built-in. ClickHouse manages a pool of long-li
- [Open House 2026 Day 2: 10 years of open source and what the ecosystem is building next](https://clickhouse.com/blog/open-house-2026-day-2): A Day 2 recap of Open House 2026 covering ClickHouse's 10 years of open source, the House Mates partner program launch, and ecosystem announcements from Fivetran, Sigma, dbt, Notion, Replit, and Google Cloud.
- [Open House observability announcements: MCP server, AI Notebooks, and ClickStack Cloud](https://clickhouse.com/blog/observability-mcp-server-ai-notebooks): At Open House 2026, we announced ClickStack Cloud in private preview, AI Notebooks in beta, and the ClickStack MCP server: three updates that make observability on ClickHouse faster to get started with, easier to investigate in, and more composable with y
- [Thank you for building with us](https://clickhouse.com/blog/thank-you-for-building-with-us): Today we welcome over 500 data engineers to our annual user conference in San Francisco and announce some exciting product launches and company milestones.
- [ClickHouse tops $250M ARR and 4,000 customers, launches Claude-powered agents at Open House 2026](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickhouse-tops-250m-arr-and-4000-customers): ClickHouse today opened Open House 2026, its second annual user conference, with a set of announcements that mark one of the company's most active quarters since founding.
- [5 countries, 12 days, one ClickHouse: inside Alexey's APJ AI Tour](https://clickhouse.com/blog/alexey-apj-ai-tour): 5 Countries, 12 Days, One ClickHouse: Inside Alexey's APJ AI tour
- [Introducing ClickStack Cloud: Serverless observability powered by ClickHouse](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickstack-cloud-private-preview): Introducing ClickStack Cloud: a fully managed, serverless observability platform built on ClickHouse where you send OpenTelemetry data to a managed endpoint and immediately explore logs, metrics, and traces without operating any infrastructure.
- [Introducing CostBench: an open benchmark for data warehouse cost-performance](https://clickhouse.com/blog/costbench-data-warehouse-cost-performance): Introducing CostBench, an open benchmark that turns cloud data warehouse runtime and billing models into comparable performance-per-dollar results.
- [Introducing House Mates: the ClickHouse partner community and program](https://clickhouse.com/blog/introducing-house-mates): We are launching House Mates, a partner community and program bringing together 60+ ISV, consulting, and channel partners to help customers build, scale, and buy ClickHouse solutions with confidence.
- [Introducing multi-stage distributed query execution in ClickHouse Cloud](https://clickhouse.com/blog/multi-stage-distributed-query-execution-clickhouse-cloud): ClickHouse Cloud introduces multi-stage distributed query execution, a new foundation for scaling single queries across many nodes and accelerating large joins and high-cardinality aggregations.
- [Open House 2026 Day 1: Real-time data without lock-in and what teams can build next](https://clickhouse.com/blog/open-house-2026-day-1): A full recap of Day 1 at Open House 2026, covering every major announcement across ClickHouse Cloud, Postgres, distributed queries, ClickPipes, ClickHouse Agents, Langfuse V4, ClickStack, and the House Mates partner program.
- [Postgres managed by ClickHouse is now in beta](https://clickhouse.com/blog/postgres-managed-by-clickhouse-beta): Postgres managed by ClickHouse is now in public beta - a fully managed, NVMe-backed Postgres service with native CDC into ClickHouse and a unified query layer via pg_clickhouse.
- [Native random sampling in ClickHouse](https://clickhouse.com/blog/native-random-sampling): Learn how to use ClickHouse's SAMPLE BY clause to run fast, approximate queries on large datasets with minimal accuracy trade-off.
- [Integrating the Rust Delta Kernel into ClickHouse](https://clickhouse.com/blog/integrating-rust-delta-kernel): How we integrated the Rust Delta Kernel to replace our native Delta Lake implementation, reducing maintenance overhead while unlocking writes, schema evolution, time travel, and partition pruning.
- [May 2026 newsletter](https://clickhouse.com/blog/202605-newsletter): Welcome to the May 2026 ClickHouse newsletter, which will round up what’s happened in real-time data warehouses over the last month.
- [clickhousectl v0.2.0: Postgres, ClickPipes and more](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickhousectl-v0-2-0-postgres-clickpipes-more): We're releasing clickhousectl v0.2.0. This release adds Postgres, ClickPipes, SQL over HTTP, a few agent-friendly output tweaks, and a standalone Rust client library for the ClickHouse Cloud API.
- [What's new in ClickStack - April 2026](https://clickhouse.com/blog/whats-new-in-clickstack-april-2026): ClickStack’s April release
- [How ChatFeatured migrated from PlanetScale Postgres to Postgres Managed by ClickHouse to power AI brand discovery](https://clickhouse.com/blog/chatfeatured): How ChatFeatured cut analytics query times from 2.5 minutes to under a second by migrating from PlanetScale Postgres to Postgres managed by ClickHouse — in just 30 minutes.
- [ClickHouse vs Prometheus for High Cardinality, Part 2: Cardinality in ClickHouse](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickhouse-vs-promethous-high-cardinality-part-2-cardinality-in-clickhouse): In this blog, we explore why high cardinality behaves fundamentally differently in column-oriented databases like ClickHouse, and why the costs appear in very different places than in traditional series-based systems like Prometheus.
- [How the D. E. Shaw group powers high-cardinality observability at scale with ClickHouse](https://clickhouse.com/blog/deshaw): How the D. E. Shaw group replaced its previous observability platform with ClickHouse to handle high-cardinality metrics at scale, achieving 7x better query performance and enabling multi-year capacity planning across millions of compute workloads.
- [ClickHouse vs Prometheus for High Cardinality, Part 1: Understanding the Problem](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickhouse-vs-promethous-high-cardinality-p1-understanding-the-problem): Why does high cardinality break Prometheus but not ClickHouse? In Part 1, we explore the architectural tradeoffs of Prometheus and other series-based systems, showing how cardinality impacts memory, ingestion, querying, and operational stability at scale.
- [Postgres FDW: Pushdown is a negotiation](https://clickhouse.com/blog/postgres-fdw-pushdown-negotiation): A deep dive into how pg_clickhouse's Foreign Data Wrapper decides what SQL to push down to ClickHouse versus execute locally in Postgres .
- [ClickStack SQL Charting and Alerting](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickstack-sql-charting-and-alerting): Learn how ClickStack’s new SQL-powered charting and alerting unlock anomaly detection, rolling baselines, and advanced observability workflows directly on top of ClickHouse, without relying on external tooling.
- [ClickHouse Cloud: Fast, Updatable Lookups with the Join Table Engine](https://clickhouse.com/blog/join-table-engine): Learn how ClickHouse Cloud's Join table engine enables fast, updatable in-memory lookups for dimensional modeling — with automatic upserts, deduplication, and data compaction powered by ReplacingMergeTree under the hood.
- [Powering self-driving vehicle analytics at Avride with ClickHouse Cloud](https://clickhouse.com/blog/avride): Avride replaced Apache Iceberg with ClickHouse Cloud, cutting index lookup latency from 20 seconds to under 100ms and ingestion from hours to seconds.
- [ClickHouse Release 26.4](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickhouse-release-26-04): ClickHouse 26.4 is here! In this release, more features become SQL compatible, COUNT DISTINCT gets faster, EXPLAIN gets even prettier, and more
- [Introducing Postgres Query Insights in ClickHouse Cloud](https://clickhouse.com/blog/postgres-query-insights-clickhouse-cloud): Query Insights is now in preview for ClickHouse Cloud Managed Postgres: every query pattern your database runs, ranked by impact, with the diagnostic picture of why each one is slow.
- [Agentic analytics starts with query-ready data: the write-side cost of Snowflake vs. ClickHouse](https://clickhouse.com/blog/write-side-cost-performance-snowflake-clickhouse): Agentic analytics makes query-readiness a write-side cost problem. This post compares Snowflake and ClickHouse under continuous ingest, showing how ClickHouse obtains query-ready data at 22× lower cost and delivers 31× better write-side cost-performance.
- [Stop guessing in production: Full fidelity tracing at scale with ClickHouse and Odigos](https://clickhouse.com/blog/odigos-full-fidelity-tracing): How ClickStack and Odigos eliminate observability gaps with zero-code eBPF instrumentation and full-fidelity distributed tracing at scale.
- [Gala supercharges analytics performance with ClickHouse on AWS](https://clickhouse.com/blog/gala): Learn how Gala migrated to the ClickHouse to improve analytics performance and cut costs
- [Goodbye limitations, hello data: How Qonto is rethinking observability with ClickHouse Cloud](https://clickhouse.com/blog/qonto): How Qonto uses ClickHouse Cloud to power observability at scale — replacing sampling and hour-capped queries with two-week query windows, 99.84% compression on high-cardinality data, and an AI incident companion built on the ClickHouse MCP server.
- [Comparing ClickHouse versions with clickhousectl](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickhousectl-compare-versions): We use clickhousectl to spin up multiple ClickHouse versions side by side and benchmark two recent performance improvements.
- [ClickHouse at Google Cloud Next '26](https://clickhouse.com/blog/google-next-2026-recap): Google Cloud Next is one of the biggest moments in the cloud calendar, and this year ClickHouse made a splash. Not just with a booth, house party and some swag, but a wave of product launches, integrations, and a deepening partnership with Google Cloud.
- [What's New in pg_clickhouse - JSONB Support, SQL value functions, Streaming, and more](https://clickhouse.com/blog/pg_clickhouse-whats-new-april-2026): The latest pg_clickhouse releases bring JSONB, date/time, and array function pushdown, plus HTTP result set streaming for lower memory usage.
- [Do you still need Elasticsearch for log analytics? ClickHouse says no.](https://clickhouse.com/blog/elasticsearch-log-analytics-clickhouse): ClickHouse now brings full-text search and large-scale analytics together in one engine, making it a powerful alternative to Elasticsearch for log analytics. This benchmark shows why.
- [ClickHouse integrates with Lakehouse Runtime Catalog](https://clickhouse.com/blog/google-lakehouse-runtime): We're excited to announce a new integration between ClickHouse and Google's Lakehouse Runtime CatalogCatalog
- [ClickHouse Cloud on Google Cloud Now Powered by Google Axion Processors: 30–55% Faster Queries, ~15% Fewer Compute Credits](https://clickhouse.com/blog/google-axion): We are migrating our Google Cloud fleet to Axion C4A instances. The results: 30–55% faster ClickBench queries and \~15% fewer compute credits across production workloads.
- [Using the ClickHouse MCP server with Google Antigravity](https://clickhouse.com/blog/google-antigravity): Learn how to connect the ClickHouse MCP server to Google Antigravity to query and visualize your data using natural language.
- [Index sharding in ClickHouse Cloud: Petabyte-scale data needs petabyte-scale indexing](https://clickhouse.com/blog/index-sharding-clickhouse-cloud-petabyte-scale-indexing): ClickHouse Cloud now shards indexes across replicas, turning a fixed per-node memory cost into a shared distributed resource. The result: lower memory usage, faster index analysis, and better performance for petabyte-scale workloads.
- [ClickHouse expands strategic collaboration with Google Cloud, bringing deeper integration, cloud flexibility, and next-generation performance](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickhouse-expands-strategic-collaboration-with-google-cloud): ClickHouse, a leader in real-time analytics, data warehousing, observability, and AI/ML, today at Google Next 26 announced a significant expansion of its strategic collaboration with Google Cloud.
- [Terraform & OpenAPI for ClickPipes is now Generally Available](https://clickhouse.com/blog/terraform-ga): Provision and manage ClickPipes resources “as code” using Terraform and OpenAPI, now with full connector coverage and improved usability
- [otel.fyi - OTel Collector docs made simple](https://clickhouse.com/blog/otel-fyi): otel.fyi is a search-first site for OpenTelemetry Collector docs, making it easy to quickly find and understand configuration for receivers, processors, exporters, and extensions without digging through scattered documentation.
- [“A generational leap”: How Trio unified payment analytics and cut storage by 88% with ClickHouse Cloud](https://clickhouse.com/blog/trio): Brazilian fintech Trio cut storage by 88% and achieved a "generational leap" in speed by building a unified payment analytics platform on ClickHouse Cloud, handling 243M+ payments and 1B+ daily events with a sliding window approach for late and duplicate
- [April 2026 newsletter](https://clickhouse.com/blog/202604-newsletter): Welcome to the April 2026 ClickHouse newsletter, which will round up what’s happened in real-time data warehouses over the last month.
- [Getting started with clickhousectl: the ClickHouse CLI for local and cloud](https://clickhouse.com/blog/getting-started-clickhousectl): A hands-on guide to clickhousectl, the ClickHouse CLI. Install it, scaffold a project, manage local servers, connect to ClickHouse Cloud, and set up CI/CD — all from your terminal.
- [Our vision for the ClickHouse Grafana plugin](https://clickhouse.com/blog/grafana-plugin-vision): We see ClickHouse and Grafana as a key part of the observability experience. Here's our vision for making the plugin more powerful and easier to use.
- [Index-based pruning in ClickHouse](https://clickhouse.com/blog/index-based-pruning): Learn how ClickHouse uses primary indexes, lightweight projections, and skip indexes to prune data before reading it. Demonstrated on a 243 million row UK property sales dataset.
- [What's new in ClickStack - March 2026](https://clickhouse.com/blog/whats-new-in-clickstack-march-2026): ClickStack’s March release introduces smarter Event Deltas, AI-powered notebooks, and full SQL chart flexibility, making investigation faster and dashboards more powerful.
- [Agentic coding with ClickHouse. One person, one data stack, one full-stack application](https://clickhouse.com/blog/agentic-coding-app): A Solutions Architect’s experience building a retail analytics platform with AI agents, real-time dashboards, and full observability on the ClickHouse data platform
- [Mintlify boosts NPS 30% and saves 60% with real-time analytics on ClickHouse Cloud](https://clickhouse.com/blog/mintlify): Mintlify replaced PostHog with ClickHouse Cloud, cutting dashboard load times from tens of seconds to under a second, eliminating rate limit errors, and achieving a 30% NPS improvement at 60% lower cost.
- [Introducing clickhousectl: the CLI for ClickHouse local and cloud (beta)](https://clickhouse.com/blog/introducing-clickhousectl-official-cli-for-clickhouse-local-and-cloud): clickhousectl is the official CLI for ClickHouse. It manages local installations, runs local servers, and operates ClickHouse Cloud. It's designed to work for humans and AI agents alike.
- [ClickHouse at FOSDEM 2026](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickhouse-at-fosdem-2026): FOSDEM 2026 took place on 31 January and 1 February in Brussels, and it was a great weekend for the ClickHouse community, both inside the conference rooms and out.
- [The three villains to agentic observability: retention, sampling and rollups](https://clickhouse.com/blog/three-villains-agentic-observability): Retention limits, sampling, and metric roll-ups aren't observability best practices - they're workarounds for storage systems that can't handle full-fidelity data, and they're becoming a hard blocker for AI-driven workflows.
- [How Eisan made POS analytics faster, cheaper, and more reliable with ClickHouse Cloud](https://clickhouse.com/blog/eisan): Rill uses ClickHouse to power real-time operational BI for 100B+ daily events, enabling instant exploration and conversational analytics directly against live datasets through a declarative, BI-as-code workflow.
- [ClickHouse Release 26.3](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickhouse-release-26-03): ClickHouse 26.3 is here! In this release, async inserts are turned on by default, we've got more JOIN reordering, materialized CTES have arrived, and more!
- [How Respan is scaling LLM observability with ClickHouse Cloud](https://clickhouse.com/blog/respan-ai-llm-observability): Respan AI uses ClickHouse Cloud to power high-throughput LLM observability across 50 million daily events. After outgrowing Postgres at 50-100 writes per second, the team migrated ingestion and analytics to ClickHouse Cloud. Incremental materialized views
- [PostgresBench: A Reproducible Benchmark for Postgres Services](https://clickhouse.com/blog/postgresbench): Discover how Postgres managed by ClickHouse compares to its peers in a reproducible, open benchmark.
- [Rill and ClickHouse: real-time operational BI for a metered world](https://clickhouse.com/blog/rill): Rill uses ClickHouse to power real-time operational BI for 100B+ daily events, enabling instant exploration and conversational analytics directly against live datasets through a declarative, BI-as-code workflow.
- [Announcing Role Based Access Control in ClickStack](https://clickhouse.com/blog/role-based-access-control-clickstack): ClickStack now supports Role-Based Access Control, giving teams precise control over who can access dashboards, searches, and notebooks. With flexible roles, fine-grained permissions, and seamless ClickHouse Cloud integration.
- [Agentic coding at ClickHouse](https://clickhouse.com/blog/agentic-coding): How to remain competitive in the AI era of software engineering
- [We taught ClickStack to read your logs like a detective novel](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickstack-read-logs-detective-novel): ClickStack gets a literary upgrade with "AI Summarize", transforming raw logs into vivid, story-driven narratives that finally explain what's really happening in your systems.
- [ClickHouse BYOC on Google Cloud now Generally Available](https://clickhouse.com/blog/byoc-gcp-ga): Run ClickHouse in your own Google Cloud account : with full data sovereignty, zero-trust networking, and a managed control plane.
- [How Padlet uses ClickHouse Cloud to power real-time classroom analytics](https://clickhouse.com/blog/padlet): Padlet uses ClickHouse Cloud to deliver real-time classroom analytics at scale, supporting billions of events per month with sub-second queries and no dedicated data team.
- [How we’re building a data platform for a new user: agents](https://clickhouse.com/blog/building-a-data-platform-for-agents): Agents need real-time ingestion, fast aggregation, flexible handling of semi-structured events, low-latency concurrency, and economics that still work at massive scale. ClickHouse already has this foundation
- [Top 10 best practices tips for ClickHouse](https://clickhouse.com/blog/10-best-practice-tips): Ten best practices for getting the most out of ClickHouse, from primary key design and data types to materialized views, ReplacingMergeTree, and join optimization — illustrated with benchmarks on a 150M row dataset.
- [More Visibility, Less Guesswork: ClickHouse Cloud's New Monitoring Capabilities](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickhouse-cloud-new-monitoring-capabilities): ClickHouse Cloud's new monitoring capabilities give platform administrators deeper visibility into their deployments, with a unified Overview page, infrastructure scaling insights, and automatic email and Slack notifications for common issues.
- [ClickHouse is data lake ready](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickhouse-is-data-lake-ready): ClickHouse now supports direct querying of Iceberg and Delta Lake formats across major cloud catalogs without requiring data migration.
- [Intelligent security at ClickHouse speed: How Cogent Security built an AI-native vulnerability management platform](https://clickhouse.com/blog/cogent-security): "The key thing that ClickHouse unlocks for AI is speed. Everything we do needs to be done at machine speed to counter AI-enabled attackers.” Karan Gugle, Founding Engineer
- [Building high-performance full-text search for object storage](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickhouse-full-text-search-object-storage): High-performance full-text search, even on object storage. This deep dive from the ClickHouse engineers explains the new text index design and how it keeps queries fast at scale.
- [Smarter Auto-Scaling for ClickHouse: The Two-Window Approach](https://clickhouse.com/blog/smarter-auto-scaling): How ClickHouse Cloud's two-window recommender and target-tracking CPU algorithm cut scale-down latency from 30 hours to 3 hours while eliminating oscillations and reducing infrastructure costs.
- [Structured Logging in .NET with Serilog and ClickHouse](https://clickhouse.com/blog/serilog): Learn how to send structured .NET logs directly to ClickHouse using Serilog — with full schema control, full-text search, and SQL queries over your log data.
- [Querying DateTimes in ClickHouse](https://clickhouse.com/blog/querying-datetimes): How to query datetime columns in ClickHouse - from hourly bucketing to rush hour analysis with real taxi data.
- [March 2026 newsletter](https://clickhouse.com/blog/202603-newsletter): Welcome to the March 2026 ClickHouse newsletter, which will round up what’s happened in real-time data warehouses over the last month.
- [How ClickStack makes ClickHouse faster for observability](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickstack-faster-observability): ClickHouse is fast by design, but raw database speed isn't enough. This post explores how ClickStack tightly integrates with ClickHouse to generate optimized queries — from progressive time window pagination and chunked charts to automatic use of materi
- [Introducing AI observability notebooks for Managed ClickStack in Private Preview](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickstack-ai-notebooks): AI-native observability notebooks for Managed ClickStack let engineers investigate logs, metrics, and traces with AI as a collaborator — keeping humans in control at every step.
- [How Socialpruf built a faster, more reliable data stack by replacing Neon with Postgres managed by ClickHouse](https://clickhouse.com/blog/socialpruf): Socialpruf migrated from Neon to Postgres managed by ClickHouse, eliminating network transfer costs and achieving up to 5x faster query performance while powering real-time social analytics dashboards that aggregate millions of rows in milliseconds.
- [AI is redrawing the database market](https://clickhouse.com/blog/ai-redrawing-database-market): AI is reshaping database market requirements across real-time analytics, data warehousing, and observability — and ClickHouse is uniquely positioned to meet them.
- [Designing the new async-native ClickHouse Python client](https://clickhouse.com/blog/python-async-native-client): clickhouse-connect v0.12.0 ships a ground-up async-native Python client using the half-sync/half-async pattern, delivering 1.16x better throughput and dramatically more stable tail latency under high concurrency.
- [ClickHouse Release 26.2](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickhouse-release-26-02): ClickHouse 26.2 is here! In this post, text-index and QBit data type become production-ready.
- [Unordered mode for GCS ClickPipes is now available](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickpipes-gcs-unordered-mode): You can now ingest data from Google Cloud Storage into ClickHouse Cloud in any order for event-driven, blazing-fast analytics.

